# 孫子 (Sun Tzu) — two choices: owner-only questions, and whose memory counts

## Answer

Q1: Adopt (a) — a question no trial can answer goes to the owner at once; in a time-boxed run it is decided provisionally at once and listed for the owner, and the run records the one line saying why no trial can answer it. Q2: Pick (a), with one correction: the report lists Claude Code's project memory present-or-absent under its own name — "harness memory for this project" — never as agent memory; it is project-scoped, not agent-scoped.

