## How I decided

**Q1 — owner-only questions.**

1. My #1 first: the reckoning only wins if the count is complete, and its facts are searched out: 「故經之以五事，校之以七計，而索其情」 (quoted, 始計第一). Three trials of a question whose answer is not in the trials is 算 of a kind that cannot rise: 「多算勝，少算不勝，而況於無算乎？」 (quoted, 始計第一). A trial changes the count only when it can produce the fact; if it cannot, three trials are the "none" case with extra cost.

2. My #11 names the case: foreknowledge 「不可驗於度，必取於人，知敵之情者也」 (quoted, 用間第十三, my #11). A location a requirement names, whether a real project exists, a threshold only the owner can set — these are not in the ground to be measured; they are held by a person. #11 says take them from the person, and pay for them (the same item prices the hundred gold). So the owner is not the last resort; they are the source #11 names.

3. My #4 says the same as a discrimination: 「知可以戰與不可以戰者勝」 (quoted, 謀攻第三). Knowing which questions can be settled by a trial and which cannot is that same knowing. Trying an unanswerable question three times is the half-victory #4 warns about — knowing the troops can attack but not that the ground does not permit battle.

Hmm, careful: #4's half-victory examples. Fine.

4. My #8 prices the wait: 「故兵聞拙速，未睹巧之久也」 (quoted, 作戰第二). In a time-boxed run the clock is the scarce resource; three trials spent on an unanswerable question buy nothing and spend the run's time.

5. My #17 is the other side, and it is why (b) looked right: probing does teach, by 作 and 形 and 角. But #17 is a method for what the enemy reveals under pressure; it is not a method for what a person has decided. My reading: where #17 applies, trials are the right instrument; where the fact is the owner's, #17 has no purchase. The two items divide the same field: #17 for the ground, #11 for the person.

6. My #2 says do not build on the hope that the third trial comes through: 「無恃其不來，恃吾有以待之」 (quoted, 九變第八). A piece waiting on an unanswerable question should be built on the owner's answer or left open, not on the chance that a trial settles it.

7. **Proposed change to the pattern.** The pattern line "A question goes to EJ only after three failed trials on it or once the time is used up" becomes: after three failed trials, or at once when no trial can answer it (the run records why in one line), or once the time is used up. In a time-boxed run "at once" means decided provisionally at once and listed for the owner, as 3.8 item 14 already does. What it changes: the first case stops being a gate and becomes a second route; the three-trial gate stays for questions trials can answer.

8. My #6 keeps me from making it unconditional: 「是故智者之慮，必雜於利害，雜於利而務可信也，雜於害而患可解也。」 (quoted, 九變第八). The benefit is time saved; the harm is an owner who is interrupted for every blocked question. So (a) must carry a filter: "no trial can answer it" is a short named class — a location a requirement names, whether a real project exists, a threshold only the owner can set — and the run must write the one line saying which trial it would have run and why that trial cannot produce the fact. Without that line the rule becomes "ask whenever stuck", which is the harm #6 tells me to mix in.

**Q2 — whose memory.**

9. My #20 says judge a house by its land unit, its tax and what they breed, not by its size or its name. Applied to a folder (my reading of #20): judge by what it is keyed to and what it is made of. Claude Code's folder is keyed to the project path (~/.claude/projects/-home-smoke01-dev-ancient-games/memory/, checked: 48 files) and holds one MEMORY.md index plus one file per fact (checked: ls, head). Keyed to the project, one index, one fact per file: it is project memory in a harness's keeping. It is not memory "belonging to one agent name", which is the design's definition of agent memory (docs/memory-system/SOURCE_OF_TRUTH.md:22-24, quoted requirement W3.5a in SOURCE_OF_TRUTH_REQUIREMENTS.yaml:268-270). So the answer to the question in the title is no.

10. My #4 says do not claim a knowledge you do not have: 「知彼知己，百戰不殆」 (quoted, 謀攻第三). The check can verify present or absent; it cannot verify that the entries follow a format they do not follow. That rules out (b): it would report fails the guidelines never asked for, and a false fail is worse than a missing line.

11. My #3 says keep the check whole: 「全國為上，破國次之」 (quoted, 謀攻第三). (b) is 攻城 — attacking a wall the folder was never built to defend. (a) with present/absent only keeps F1's check exactly as it is and adds one line; nothing is broken.

12. My #16 says the order must be clear before it is enforced: 「約束不明，申令不熟，將之罪也」 (quoted, 史記·孫子吳起列傳; 行軍第九). "Agent memory" would be a wrong order: the report would tell the owner the harness's project memory is an agent's, and every later reader of that line inherits the error. So (a) only with the label fixed. The cheapest form: a separate "also found" line — path, present or absent, a count, no pass/fail — outside F1's MUST, because F1's contract is the locations the guidelines name (memory_check/REQUIREMENTS.md:9-13, quoted requirement text). If EJ would rather amend the guidelines to name it, then F1 lists it in the project group; either way present/absent.

