Costs and risks:
Q1:
- Owner attention becomes a shared resource; a loose definition of "no trial can answer it" turns every blocked agent into an interruption, and a flood of questions is the harm side of #6.
- A question wrongly classed unanswerable stops the run's own search too early; the run may never find a fact a trial could have produced (my #17 — the trial that would have taught is not run).
